WEBVTT

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:17.630
Hello...

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:21.540
What happened, Touma? What's with that appearance?

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:24.240
It was raining really hard on the way here.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.160
Never mind that, so take them off! You'll get a cold!

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.680
Kana, get the bath ready!

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:31.180
Okay!

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:39.960
This is heavenly.

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:54.020
Ah, that felt so good!

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:57.240
Touma!

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:57.950
Huh?

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:03.140
Here you go, cocoa. It will warm you up.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:05.140
Wow, thanks Haruka!

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:09.750
Delicious!

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:12.820
Jeez, Touma.

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:16.360
You really cause some trouble.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:19.780
I feel like a king from top to bottom!

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:25.970
Oh yeah, Chiaki. Lend me some clothes.

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:31.220
What's with that attitude? There are other ways to ask, aren't there?

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.710
That's right... These won't dry soon.

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:39.730
Haruka-neesama!

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:41.730
Hmm? What is it, Chiaki?

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.420
Please leave this to me.

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:49.320
I'll beat into Touma how the youngest child should behave!

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:53.770
Eh? Ah... then please take care of the rest, okay?

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.820
Kana, when is Fujioka coming?

00:01:57.980 --> 00:01:59.370
Eh? Fujioka?

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:01.880
Huh? Soon, I think.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:03.880
Hey, Chiaki, I said lend me some clothes.

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:06.220
At this rate, it will be a little...

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:07.470
Not a chance.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:08.020
W-

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:10.450
Chiaki, lend me-

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:11.220
No.

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:15.110
This is real harrassment!

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:20.060
Come to think of it, Natsuki was talking about this yesterday.

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:27.070
Pretty good, Touma.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:30.460
Take this! And that! How's that?!

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:34.900
All right!

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:37.820
You're weak, Natsuki.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:41.100
Touma!

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:41.590
Huh?

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:43.760
Lend me that game-center-type thing.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:45.310
This?

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:49.940
Okay Touma. One more match.

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:07.440
Game and set.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:09.280
Touma.

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:09.900
Huh?

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:14.470
Men should return both debts and grudges twofold.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:22.440
That's why, as a man, I will retaliate by taking those clothes off of you!

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:23.380
What?

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:26.960
You're a girl, so you'll be in trouble if you don't have any clothes, right?

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:31.660
It's okay Touma. I'll lend you my clothes.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:43.190
Coming!

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:48.500
Ah, Chiaki! Lend me some clothes!

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:49.750
No-wa-y.

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:52.990
Oh man...

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:55.060
What a downpour.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.460
Ah. Hi, Minami.

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:00.140
Oh, it's just you?

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:02.810
Oh well. Come in.

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:05.140
Sorry to trouble you.

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:07.620
Hurry up and lend them to me, Chiaki!

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:08.610
I said no way, didn't I?

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:08.990
Fine, then these will do!
I said no way, didn't I?

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:10.480
Fine, then these will do!

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:11.160
What are you doing?

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:12.100
S-Stop!
What are you doing?

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:12.850
S-Stop!

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:15.750
Shut up! I'll kill you!

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:17.780
Stop it, Touma!

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:18.380
What are you doing, Touma?
Stop it, Touma!

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:19.180
What are you doing, Touma?

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:20.530
Fujioka!

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:24.800
I beg you, Chiaki-sama! Please lend me some clothes!

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:26.180
I was wrong!

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:30.300
Oh, good girl. So you can ask properly after all.

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:32.300
Come to my room.

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:35.030
So it was okay if I'd just asked properly?

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:40.760
Fujioka!

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:41.270
Huh?

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:46.040
Don't think that this has nothing to do with you! Watch that attitude of yours!

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:51.490
Wh-What was that supposed to mean?

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:55.180
Oh! Welcome, Fujioka-kun!

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:56.970
Huh... What?

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:01.840
Woah! Even though Haruka said "welcome"... what's with that attitude?!

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:02.600
Huh?!

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:05.040
Oh no! Fujioka-kun is the same!

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:09.410
You're right! Okay, undress, undress. Take a bath first.

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:11.850
Wh-What are you doing?

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:50.370
This sweet is so pretty!

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:52.690
It's just like a jewel!

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:54.690
It's so red!

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:55.920
It's red.

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:04.870
They use colors from insects in natural food coloring, you know?

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:16.580
Calm down, Uchida. It's okay.

00:07:16.690 --> 00:07:17.370
Huh?

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:18.540
Probably.

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:23.870
Uchida!

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.860
Get rid of it yourself.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:35.130
It came out.

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:37.130
That was mean.

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:40.710
Chiaki, you hurt people with your vast knowledge.

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:45.690
Chiaki, tell us something that won't hurt anyone.

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:49.280
Okay. Speaking of insects...

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.450
Got it. The black ant.

00:07:53.170 --> 00:07:53.820
Huh?

00:07:55.140 --> 00:08:00.190
At the start of spring during May and June on the day after the rain clears,

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:03.860
the male and female black ants that have grown wings

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:08.760
fly out of their hives and engage in a mating swarm. And then...

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:09.030
Chiaki.
fly out of their hives and engage in a mating swarm. And then...

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:09.580
Chiaki.

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:09.880
Huh?

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:11.880
I'm listening, but...

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:13.880
Are you going to continue this story?

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:32.700
To have a marriage ceremony in the sky... that's a pretty wonderful thing.

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:38.370
Is it over?

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:42.210
Yeah. The princess has been completely offended.

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:46.650
But...!

00:08:47.180 --> 00:08:49.730
Let me tell you one thing about Chiaki.

00:08:50.020 --> 00:08:51.250
Huh? What's that?

00:08:51.890 --> 00:08:54.800
If people don't listen to her stories, she gets angry.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:56.510
Huh? But that's normal.

00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:04.660
By the way, here's something about me. I can tell who it is from the way they ring the bell.

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:05.770
Really?

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:08.420
That sound means...

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:10.420
Yoshino has come!

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:11.510
Yoshino has?

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:23.160
I said Fujioka was here just now, didn't I?

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:24.390
No, you didn't!

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:29.940
Hello, Chiaki-chan!

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:32.710
Chiaki-chan?

00:09:38.730 --> 00:09:39.750
Chiaki-chan.

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:40.110
Huh?

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:41.810
Look outside.

00:09:42.230 --> 00:09:42.520
Oh.

00:09:52.310 --> 00:09:53.840
A contrail?

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:55.840
Chiaki.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:00.980
Don't tell me you're going to hurt your beloved Fujioka-kun with your knowledge?

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:02.750
Fujioka.

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:03.170
Huh?

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:07.570
Contrails are produced when a component of the exhaust fumes

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:09.780
suddenly cool down and condense.

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:12.950
It's not smoke. It's exactly like a cloud.

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:16.790
It's a cloud made by people.

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:18.570
Wow...

00:10:29.410 --> 00:10:30.290
Why?!

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:34.700
Why did you talk about horrible stuff when it was to me?!

00:10:34.890 --> 00:10:36.320
What's with that atmosphere?!

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:41.300
Uchida, that's not part of the atmosphere, it's a contrail...

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:44.200
No! I'm not talking about that kind of atmosphere!

00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:46.790
Everyone, look! It's exhaust fumes!

00:10:47.150 --> 00:10:48.790
I told you, those are clouds!

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:08.990
During the holiday the other day, I went to a department store with Haruka-neesama and Kana...

00:11:08.990 --> 00:11:12.360
We do we have homework during the holidays?

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:18.950
Who knows? The only thing I know is that I don't understand these problems.

00:11:18.950 --> 00:11:20.370
The food was delicious, wasn't it?

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:20.970
Yeah.

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:25.020
Chiaki really likes Fujioka-kun, doesn't she?

00:11:25.270 --> 00:11:27.890
Huh? I guess so.

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:31.200
But he's like Chiaki's reserved seat.

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:33.200
That's okay, but...

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:33.910
Huh?

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:40.460
Around the time that I met Fujioka, thanks to him, I had some really bad experiences.

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:48.100
No. That should be 3-5-2.

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:52.670
What are you saying? In that scenario, 3-6-1 is correct.

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:56.760
You could also push forward by playing 3-4-3.

00:11:57.660 --> 00:11:59.830
I think that's pushing forward too hard.

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:00.580
Kana, what on earth is going on here?
I think that's pushing forward too hard.

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:02.400
Kana, what on earth is going on here?

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:08.790
It looks like, while you were changing, Touma and Fujioka got into a conversation about soccer.

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:09.760
You might be right...

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:17.790
The best thing was when they played a long ball and made space between those two.

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:22.570
If you're talking about that, I think the cross just before it was perfect.

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:29.340
I don't really understand what they're talking about but they're acting pretty lively.

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:34.980
Touma. Come here a second.

00:12:35.470 --> 00:12:36.410
Time out.

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:41.000
Don't forget to add lost time afterwards.

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:42.070
Of course!

00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:46.730
What is it, Chiaki?

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:53.700
Er... Oh yeah. Have you introduced yourself properly to Fujioka yet?

00:12:54.550 --> 00:12:55.700
Not yet!

00:13:00.940 --> 00:13:03.590
I'm Touma. I play forward.

00:13:04.250 --> 00:13:06.870
I'm Fujioka. I play anywhere.

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:09.430
Anywhere? That's amazing!

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:10.640
Not really.

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:13.480
No, I think it is! It's really cool!

00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:16.470
Touma! Touma!

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:18.600
Time out.

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:19.370
Sure.

00:13:19.430 --> 00:13:22.010
Kana, please record how much time we lose.

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:23.140
Sure.

00:13:24.790 --> 00:13:25.550
What's wrong?

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:30.310
Have you talked to Fujioka about your gender?

00:13:30.420 --> 00:13:31.070
Huh?

00:13:31.670 --> 00:13:34.800
Touma became Chiaki's little brother just recently.

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:36.960
Eh, really?

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:38.520
So have you?

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:42.460
I... haven't really spoken to him about it...

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:45.690
All right, Touma, act like a guy in front of Fujioka!

00:13:45.790 --> 00:13:46.840
Huh?

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:52.820
You've gotten excited about soccer, so as a man, you should have a friendly wrestle...

00:13:53.980 --> 00:13:56.750
What's wrong Chiaki? You're acting strangely today.

00:13:56.810 --> 00:13:58.930
Huh? I'm not acting strangely!

00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:05.490
Anyway, that's my seat.

00:14:06.040 --> 00:14:06.670
Move away.

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:08.670
Oh, I see.

00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:10.860
Fujioka!

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:11.470
Yeah.

00:14:12.430 --> 00:14:16.070
This is Chiaki's seat, so could you move over there a little?

00:14:16.310 --> 00:14:18.500
That's not what I meant!

00:14:18.550 --> 00:14:21.170
What is it? What do you want me to do?

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:40.420
What? You want to start something?

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:40.800
Yeah, you idiot!
What? You want to start something?

00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:42.120
Yeah, you idiot!

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:43.570
Why you...!

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:44.780
Stop it, Touma!

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:47.170
What are you doing? Let go of me!

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:49.900
Don't be violent to girls!

00:14:49.960 --> 00:14:50.610
Huh?

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:57.060
Furthermore, you may have confidence about your soccer, but you've got excess fat on your chest, haven't you?

00:15:01.610 --> 00:15:02.130
Touma!

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:03.110
Y-Yes!

00:15:03.910 --> 00:15:06.340
I'll help you get your mind and body into shape!

00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:07.130
Huh?

00:15:08.490 --> 00:15:10.090
What should I do, Chiaki?

00:15:12.150 --> 00:15:13.360
It's special training, Touma!

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:15.760
N-No way!

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:27.900
Erm, I think that's an example of a middle through-pass.

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:29.370
Through-pass?

00:15:29.940 --> 00:15:33.300
Then what was that "branch" you were talking about just now?

00:15:33.810 --> 00:15:36.150
That was referring to a defensive midfielder.

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:39.860
Touma knows all about this stuff, doesn't she?

00:15:40.010 --> 00:15:42.520
Speaking of which, Touma isn't here today, is she?

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:45.560
Did something happen with Touma?

00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:48.030
No... Not really.

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:56.600
What's wrong, Touma?

00:15:57.860 --> 00:15:59.160
Oh, it's you, Chiaki.

00:16:00.130 --> 00:16:04.060
It's because of that special training. The special training! I was summoned early in the morning for it.

00:16:04.160 --> 00:16:06.590
Erm, what was it now?

00:16:07.170 --> 00:16:11.040
"A soccer match with Chiaki's little brother."

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:14.120
Ah! What a pain.

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:18.720
Then don't go to the training!

00:16:18.770 --> 00:16:22.880
Eh? Oh yeah, why don't you come along next time, Chiaki?

00:16:24.740 --> 00:16:27.020
I'll do it when I put on some more fat!

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:33.400
And then at the department store, Haruka-neesama...

00:16:33.580 --> 00:16:34.230
Yeah, yeah.

00:16:35.270 --> 00:16:40.910
It's terrible. For a long time after that, I carried on going to the morning practice.

00:16:41.130 --> 00:16:42.780
R-Really?

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.640
And in the end, Chiaki didn't come either.

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:49.650
Oh well, it seems like Chiaki is bad at sport.

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:51.450
It can't be helped, I guess.

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:53.550
Huh, really?

00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:37.390
Natsuki, if you're going to request something, that manner of speech is not appropriate.

00:18:37.700 --> 00:18:40.040
If I'm outside, I can do it properly.

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:40.850
That's too optimistic!

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:44.120
At some point, your usual manner of speech will come out.

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:45.510
I know that.

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:48.750
Manners are important to Minami-san, aren't they?

00:18:49.050 --> 00:18:51.590
Also, that's not a good face to put on.

00:18:51.770 --> 00:18:53.740
This is the best I can do!

00:18:53.740 --> 00:18:57.960
Well, like your eyes, that's not a face that's making a request.

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:00.510
Smile, smile!

00:19:00.850 --> 00:19:03.540
Oh. My manner of speech and a smile.

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:10.500
I don't really get it, but if you're going to ask Haruka for something, what you have to be careful of is Chiaki.

00:19:10.800 --> 00:19:11.140
Huh?

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:16.610
It's a pain to pay attention to Chiaki. If you ignore her, Haruka will get a bad impression.

00:19:16.950 --> 00:19:17.950
Don't ignore her.

00:19:18.390 --> 00:19:20.220
Is Chiaki the one who ties her hair?

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:26.200
That's Kana. Paying attention to Kana can get complicated, so where possible, you ought to avoid it.

00:19:26.760 --> 00:19:28.200
I feel bad about it though.

00:19:39.460 --> 00:19:42.360
Expression and a smile... huh?

00:19:45.130 --> 00:19:48.810
I have come on this fine day to ask a favour of you.

00:19:51.320 --> 00:19:55.140
Although I am unworthy, please accept this.

00:20:00.230 --> 00:20:03.630
Hey, Chiaki, are yeast buns really something you call unworthy?

00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:05.960
You'd usually call them steamed.

00:20:06.280 --> 00:20:11.150
My request has to do with Touma.

00:20:11.450 --> 00:20:15.240
Oh, I see. If it's just about Touma, there shouldn't be a problem.

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:18.240
Smile, smile!

00:20:29.960 --> 00:20:36.070
Touma's been coming home a little late, so I wonder if you could say something to her for me.

00:20:36.320 --> 00:20:38.700
That grin just now...

00:20:40.360 --> 00:20:42.630
Have you talked to Touma properly yourselves?

00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:48.740
Paying attention to Kana can get complicated, so where possible, you ought to avoid it.

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:50.510
Hey, have you?

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:04.520
What going on? He's only looking at Haruka!

00:21:04.920 --> 00:21:08.870
Is he aiming for Haruka-neesama? I don't approve!

00:21:09.270 --> 00:21:11.530
Have you spoken to Touma yourself?!

00:21:20.280 --> 00:21:23.570
If you ignore Chiaki, Haruka will get a bad impression.

00:21:24.550 --> 00:21:25.570
Don't ignore her.

00:21:36.870 --> 00:21:38.840
Have you spoken to Touma yourself?

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:43.330
I have, but it's fallen upon deaf ears. It's not an easy thing to do.

00:21:47.940 --> 00:21:51.340
Then why don't you just be firm with her?!

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:53.610
Woof! Woof, woof, woof!

00:22:00.580 --> 00:22:02.670
You can just be a little more firm with her, can't you?

00:22:02.970 --> 00:22:05.640
I have spoken firmly with her, but it was useless.

00:22:08.880 --> 00:22:11.520
Hold it! Are you listening to me at all?!

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:12.920
Woof, woof, woof!

00:22:18.460 --> 00:22:21.740
In that case, I'll try saying something.

00:22:22.020 --> 00:22:23.130
Please.

00:22:24.110 --> 00:22:28.220
Touma, won't you go home a little earlier from now on?

00:22:28.840 --> 00:22:29.250
Huh?

00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:42.220
Well... if you're the one asking, Haruka, then I will.

00:22:48.890 --> 00:22:53.220
And so it has been decided that she will come home thirty minutes earlier.

00:22:54.250 --> 00:22:57.230
You see? Your manner of speech is the most important thing.

00:22:57.460 --> 00:22:59.230
No, it's definitely the smile.

00:22:59.380 --> 00:23:00.990
No, no, the expression is.

00:23:01.490 --> 00:23:02.990
No, no, the smile is.

00:23:03.630 --> 00:23:07.490
So what you wanted to ask about was the time I come home?

00:23:20.610 --> 00:23:21.880
Erm, excuse me.

00:23:22.700 --> 00:23:26.590
Although I am unworthy, please give me this lettuce.

00:23:31.430 --> 00:23:34.410
Chiaki, you really saved me! Thank you!

00:23:34.450 --> 00:23:36.940
You could have just said that right at the beginning, you idiot.

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:38.830
I was in a real pinch there!

00:23:38.840 --> 00:23:42.350
Next time on Minamike Okaeri: Nice Image

00:23:42.350 --> 00:23:42.530
What do you mean, someone else's business?
Next time on Minamike Okaeri: Nice Image

00:23:42.530 --> 00:23:43.930
What do you mean, someone else's business?

00:23:43.960 --> 00:23:44.810
What is it?
